    "updated_at": "2016-09-02T06:40:56Z",
    "body": "A new potential attack I see is that if an attacker somehow gets to add request headers and those request headers do something at the redirect level (or turn a response into a redirect) there's a new vulnerability of sorts that you cannot have today. Not sure how much of a deal-breaker that should be.\n",
