    "updated_at": "2016-09-02T15:37:32Z",
    "body": "Ah I see. Although it sounds like in this case server explicitly wants to change redirect URL based on metadata it received in own request headers, so doesn't seem like vulnerability, rather as a part of the feature (custom response based on request headers). With the same luck server can do that based on URL query parameters.\n",
